  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 905.08 Obligations and Responsibilities of Certified Individuals",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 905.08 Obligations and Responsibilities of Certified Individuals. Each individual certified under this part shall:\n\n(a) Undertake or supervise work performed pursuant to RSA 482-A:3, XVII;\n\n(b) Use reasonable care, judgment, and application of his or her knowledge when maintaining, repairing, replacing, or modifying a culvert;\n\n(c) Not submit any information that is false, incomplete, or misleading on, in, or with any application for an initial or renewal certificate or quarterly report;\n\n(d) Repair, replace, or modify each culvert in compliance with:\n\n(1) RSA 482-A, exclusive of the requirement to obtain a permit;\n\n(2) Env-Wt 100 et seq., exclusive of the requirements pertaining to applying for and obtaining a permit; and\n\n(3) Best management practices to protect water quality; and\n\n(e) Correct any work that is identified as defective by the department or by the state or municipal public works agency for which the work was performed.\n\nSource. #12809, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt900.html"
